@* Three photographs fanned out (FX162, the design page's "Three businesses, three agents"): the one in the middle
   stands forward, the two beside it turn in. Each stands in a glass window with the three dots and its business's
   address in the bar, holding its photograph and caption alone (FX167); the one picked or shown comes to the front.
   A site gives them as records (ADR 0125). *@
<div class="shot-fan">
    @for (var index = 0; index < Items.Count; index++)
    {
        var shot = Items[index];
        <a class="@PlaceOf(index)" href="@shot.Href" data-reflect="@Reflect" id="@AddressOf(shot)" data-piece="@Pick">
            <FramedWindow Address="@shot.Address">
                <img src="@shot.Image" alt="" loading="lazy" />
                <span class="shot-caption"><b>@shot.Title</b>@shot.Line</span>
            </FramedWindow>
        </a>
    }
</div>
